{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Which I hewed for myself.</b> In its plain sense, like ״כִּי יִכְרֶה אִישׁ.״ And its midrash further settles the language, like ״אֲשֶׁר קָנִיתִי״ — R. Yehudah says: when I went to the maritime cities they called a purchase כִּירָה. And its midrash yet further: a term of כְּרִי דָגוּר, that Ya'akov took all the silver and gold he brought from the house of Lavan and made it into a heap (כְּרִי) and said to Esav: take this in place of your portion in the cave."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {0 "Rashi cites R. Yehudah by the Aramaic epithet אָרַ\"עֲ (= אָרֵי עֵינָא, 'eyes of the sages' or possibly thetranslator's sigil for Rabbi Yehudah); resolved by convention as R. Yehudah."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:26.399257713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}